Leetcode-345.-Reverse-Vowels-of-a-String
Description
Given a string s, reverse only all the vowels in the string and return it.

The vowels are 'a', 'e', 'i', 'o', and 'u', and they can appear in both lower and upper cases, more than once

Solution
Vowels are special alphabets :'a', 'e', 'i', 'o', and 'u'.

We have been given a string s and our aim is to reverse the string in which vowels will be swapped or reversed . Meanwhile the rest of the elements remains in place.

Example:

Input: s = "IceCreAm"

Output: "AceCreIm"

Explanation:

The vowels in s are ['I', 'e', 'e', 'A']. On reversing the vowels, s becomes "AceCreIm".

Algorithm
Initialise 2 pointers l and r as 0 and len(nums)-1 respectively.
Create a set of vowels consisting of both uppercase and lowercase characters.
Convert the string s to list so that we can perform operations on each character individually.
Use a while loop until l<r
If the right pointer character is not in vowels set ,then decrement r by 1 to search for other vowels.
If the left pointer character is not in vowels set ,then increment l by 1 to search for other vowels.
Else swap the r and l characters . Increment l by 1 , decrement r by 1.
Now when all operatiosn are done , join the list again to a string.
Code
class Solution:

def reverseVowels(self, s: str) -> str:
    vowels={'a', 'e', 'i', 'o','u','A','E','I','O','U'}
    l=0
    r=len(s)-1
    s=list(s)
    while l<=r:
        
        if s[l] not in vowels:
            l+=1
        elif s[r] not in vowels:
            r-=1
        else :
            s[l],s[r]=s[r],s[l]
            l+=1
            r-=1
    return "".join(s)
Complexity
Time Complexity:

Each character of the string is checked at most once by either the left (l) or right (r) pointer.

Even though there are some if checks, they are constant-time operations (O(1)).

Hence, the overall time complexity is:

O(n)

where n = length of the string.

Space Complexity:

We convert the string into a list to allow swapping → requires O(n) extra space.

The vowels set is constant in size (10 elements: 5 lowercase + 5 uppercase), so that’s O(1) space.

So the total space complexity is:

O(n)
